chum in the lakshan was shot by police  on tuesday during a fuel shortage  protest a friend of the 42 year old  father of two explains what he saw  i saw him running after trying to  retrieve his bicycle  then the policeman shot him he fell on  the ground and then i saw the same  policeman chasing people and firing a  senior officer was telling them to keep  firing and they did  lakshan was the family's main  breadwinner his wife priyangani and two  teenage children are in shock  i will be waiting till justice is done  for what happened to my husband i don't  know if that'll happen but it should  someday right  what happened to me mustn't happen to  another person  protesters rallied in rambukhana earlier  this week to condemn the shortage of  fuel and large increases in the price of  essential items  tensions escalated as police attempted  to disperse the crowd a police commander  has admitted giving the order to shoot  casualties were rushed to hospital the  shooting has raised concerns both here  and abroad with the police chief being  summoned before the human rights  commission  a senior buddhist priest at the funeral  condemned the killing  it's because of the wrongful actions of  an extremely immoral and extremely  selfish government that has allowed  lawlessness to reign and that lakshan  lost his life these rulers have no  understanding of good and evil that's  why they've made fraud corruption and  robbery their power and strength  following widespread protests against  the island's worst economic crisis since  independence 74 years ago president  gotaber rajapaksa has reshuffled his  cabinet  choosing a majority of new faces he's  also admitted to making several mistakes  but for more sri lankans it comes too  late  protests are continuing around the  country by thousands of people like  charming the lakshan who had been trying  for days to obtain fuel for his lorry  which he used to make a living  rather than scare people away protesters  say his death will only serve to make  their fight stronger to get the  government to go minil fernandez al  jazeera rambo kana
 

